.TH VTPM-MDS-BIND 8 "October 2026" "vtpm-mds" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
vtpm-mds-bind \- bind guest ports of the IMDS bridge to their configured MAC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vtpm-mds-bind
.RB [ \-bridge
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-pve-root
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-nft
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-run-dir
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-print ]
.RB [ \-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vtpm-mds
identifies a guest by the MAC address behind its IP address.
.B vtpm-mds-bind
keeps the nftables table
.B bridge vtpm_mds_bind
so that, for every NIC of a guest of this node that is attached to the IMDS
bridge, frames from its port
.BI tap <vmid> i <n>
are dropped when their source MAC is not the one in the guest's configuration,
and ARP packets are dropped when their sender MAC is not.
NICs on other bridges are not touched.
.PP
It reads
.IR /etc/pve/local/qemu-server/*.conf
every five seconds, rewrites the table in one transaction when the bound ports
change, and restores the table when it is missing or was changed by anything
else, for example after
.BR "systemctl restart nftables" .
When it stops, the table stays as it was; removing the package deletes it.
.PP
If the first check leaves no table, because the configurations cannot be
read or the apply fails, it exits non-zero and systemd restarts it. Twelve
failures within a minute leave the unit
.BR failed ,
and it stays failed after the cause is fixed. Within that minute systemd
refuses
.B systemctl start vtpm-mds-bind
as well; run
.B systemctl reset-failed vtpm-mds-bind
first, or start it once the minute has passed. A failure after a successful start does not stop it: it retries every
five seconds and logs when the error changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-bridge " name"
The IMDS bridge. Default
.BR vmbr_imds .
.TP
.BI \-pve-root " path"
The Proxmox cluster filesystem. Default
.IR /etc/pve .
.TP
.BI \-nft " path"
The nft binary. Default
.IR /usr/sbin/nft .
.TP
.BI \-run-dir " path"
Where the last applied script is written as
.IR vtpm_mds_bind.nft .
Default
.BR $RUNTIME_DIRECTORY ,
which the unit sets to
.IR /run/vtpm-mds-bind .
.TP
.B \-print
Print the table for the current configurations and exit, changing nothing.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/vtpm-mds-bind.service
Runs the binder as user
.B vtpm-mds
with
.B CAP_NET_ADMIN
only.
.TP
.I /run/vtpm-mds-bind/vtpm_mds_bind.nft
The last applied script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vtpm-mds (8),
.BR nft (8)
